.TH SCD-REPORT 1 "2026-11-10" "SCD Reporting 1.0.0" "SCD Reporting"
.SH NAME
scd\-report \- run an SCD Reporting report and download it
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scd\-report
[\fB\-s\fR \fITEXT\fR] [\fB\-a\fR \fIEMAIL\fR] [\fB\-p\fR \fISLUG\fR]... [\fB\-\-category\fR \fISLUG\fR]... [\fB\-\-lab\-priority\fR \fISLUG\fR]... [\fB\-g\fR \fISLUG\fR] [\fB\-\-employee\-group\fR \fISLUG\fR] [\fB\-\-entry\-type\fR \fISLUG\fR] [\fB\-\-from\fR \fIDATE\fR] [\fB\-\-to\fR \fIDATE\fR] [\fB\-\-period\fR \fINAME\fR] [\fB\-\-overlap\fR] [\fB\-\-private\-only\fR | \fB\-\-exclude\-private\fR] [\fB\-\-archived\fR] [\fB\-\-id\fR \fIID\fR]... [\fB\-f\fR \fIFORMAT\fR] [\fB\-o\fR \fIFILE\fR | \fB\-O\fR] [\fB\-\-count\fR] [\fB\-c\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-u\fR \fIURL\fR] [\fB\-t\fR \fITOKEN\fR] [\fB\-\-token\-file\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fISEC\fR] [\fB\-\-ca\-bundle\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-k\fR] [\fB\-v\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs the same report as the web Reports page through \fBPOST /api/reports/\fR and writes it in
the chosen format. The server applies your role's scope exactly as the page does: Group Leaders see
their own group, Division Heads their managed groups, Functional Leads their managed projects;
division-head-only entries are hidden unless you are an Admin or Division Head.
.PP
Requires the Auditor, Group Leader, Division Head, Functional Lead or Admin role; others get HTTP 403.
Every export is recorded in the audit log with \fBsource: api\fR.
.PP
With no filters the report covers every current (unarchived) entry in your scope.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-f " FORMAT" "\fR, \fP\-\-format " FORMAT
\fBmd\fR (default, or \fB$SCD_FORMAT\fR / config \fBformat\fR), \fBtxt\fR, \fBcsv\fR, \fBjson\fR,
\fBxlsx\fR or \fBpdf\fR. \fBxlsx\fR and \fBpdf\fR are binary and are refused on a terminal; use
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-O\fR or a redirect. \fBjson\fR is the flat row format of the web download (one object
per entry with project, category and tag names joined into strings).
.TP
.BI \-o " FILE" "\fR, \fP\-\-output " FILE
Write to \fIFILE\fR instead of standard output (\fB\-\fR means standard output).
.TP
.BR \-O ", " \-\-remote\-name
Write to the file name the server suggests (e.g. \fBscd_report_20261110_1432.md\fR) in the
current directory.
.TP
.B \-\-count
Print only the number of matching entries. Not audited.
.SH FILTER OPTIONS
These are the filters of the web Reports page. Taxonomy values take a slug or a numeric id
(list them with \fBscd\-taxonomy\fR(1)); options marked ... may be repeated, and a single value
may also be comma-separated (\fB\-p dune,nova\fR). Repeated values of one option match
\fIany\fR of them; different options are combined with AND. An unknown slug is an error, not an
empty result.
.TP
.BI \-s " TEXT" "\fR, \fP\-\-search " TEXT
Search title and description. Words are ORed by default; \fBAND\fR, \fBOR\fR and \fBXOR\fR
operators and "quoted phrases" are honoured, evaluated left to right.
.TP
.BI \-a " EMAIL" "\fR, \fP\-\-author " EMAIL
Author email, case-insensitive substring match.
.TP
.BI \-p " SLUG" "\fR, \fP\-\-project " SLUG
Project. Repeatable.
.TP
.BI \-\-category " SLUG"
Category. Repeatable.
.TP
.BI \-\-lab\-priority " SLUG"
Lab priority. Repeatable.
.TP
.BI \-g " SLUG" "\fR, \fP\-\-group " SLUG
Activity group recorded on the entry.
.TP
.BI \-\-employee\-group " SLUG"
The author's own group.
.TP
.BI \-\-entry\-type " SLUG"
Entry type.
.TP
.BI \-\-from " DATE" "\fR, \fP\-\-to " DATE
Range start and end, \fBYYYY\-MM\-DD\fR. By default an entry matches only if its period lies
entirely inside the range.
.TP
.BI \-\-period " NAME"
A named range relative to today: \fBtoday\fR, \fBthis\-week\fR, \fBlast\-week\fR (weeks start Monday),
\fBthis\-month\fR, \fBlast\-month\fR, \fBthis\-quarter\fR, \fBlast\-quarter\fR
(calendar quarters), \fBthis\-year\fR, \fBlast\-year\fR.
An explicit \fB\-\-from\fR or \fB\-\-to\fR replaces that end of the named range.
.TP
.B \-\-overlap
Match entries whose period overlaps the range instead of lying entirely within it.
.TP
.BR \-\-private\-only ", " \-\-exclude\-private
Only private entries, or no private entries.
.TP
.B \-\-archived
Archived entries instead of current ones.
.TP
.BI \-\-id " ID"
Restrict to these entry ids. Repeatable.
.SH CONNECTION OPTIONS
These override the environment, \fB.env\fR files and the config file.
.TP
.BI \-c " FILE" "\fR, \fP\-\-config " FILE
YAML config file. Default: \fB$SCD_CONFIG\fR, else
\fI~/.config/scd\-reporting/config.yaml\fR. Naming a file that does not exist is an error.
.TP
.BI \-u " URL" "\fR, \fP\-\-url " URL
Server root URL, e.g. \fBhttps://scd\-reporting.fnal.gov\fR.
.TP
.BI \-t " TOKEN" "\fR, \fP\-\-token " TOKEN
API token (Profile \(-> API Token). Prefer \fB\-\-token\-file\fR or the config file:
a token on the command line is visible in the process list and shell history.
.TP
.BI \-\-token\-file " FILE"
Read the token from \fIFILE\fR (used only when no token is set by a higher-priority source).
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " SEC"
Request timeout in seconds (default 300; AI summaries can take minutes).
.TP
.BI \-\-ca\-bundle " FILE"
PEM file of CA certificates used to verify the server.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-insecure
Do not verify the server's TLS certificate. Testing only.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Log each request URL and the response status, type and size to standard error.
The token is never logged.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the client version.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Settings are resolved per key in this order, highest first:
.IP 1. 4
command-line options;
.IP 2. 4
environment variables;
.IP 3. 4
\fB.env\fR files: \fI./.env\fR, then \fI~/.config/scd\-reporting/.env\fR (only \fBSCD_*\fR keys are read;
the current directory's file wins);
.IP 4. 4
the YAML config file;
.IP 5. 4
built-in defaults.
.PP
Config file keys are \fBurl\fR, \fBtoken\fR, \fBtoken_file\fR, \fBtimeout\fR, \fBca_bundle\fR,
\fBinsecure\fR and \fBformat\fR. The file is shared with \fBscd\-post\-entry\fR(1).
Example (see \fIconfig/scd\-client.yaml.example\fR):
.PP
.nf
.RS
url: https://scd\-reporting.fnal.gov
token_file: ~/.config/scd\-reporting/token
format: md
timeout: 300
.RE
.fi
.PP
Run \fBscd\-whoami \-\-settings\fR to see each resolved value and where it came from.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SCD_URL
Server root URL.
.TP
.B SCD_TOKEN
API token.
.TP
.B SCD_TOKEN_FILE
File containing the API token.
.TP
.B SCD_CONFIG
Path of the YAML config file.
.TP
.B SCD_TIMEOUT
Request timeout in seconds.
.TP
.B SCD_CA_BUNDLE
CA certificate bundle.
.TP
.B SCD_INSECURE
\fB1\fR/\fBtrue\fR/\fByes\fR disables TLS verification.
.TP
.B SCD_FORMAT
Default output format of \fBscd\-report\fR(1).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The server rejected the request (HTTP 4xx/5xx). The status and the server's message, including
per-field errors, are printed to standard error. 401 means the token is missing, wrong, revoked
or belongs to a deactivated account; 403 means your role does not allow the request.
.TP
.B 2
Usage or configuration error (no URL or token, bad option, missing config file, binary output to a
terminal).
.TP
.B 3
The server could not be reached (DNS, connection refused, TLS failure, timeout).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/scd\-reporting/config.yaml
Default config file.
.TP
.I ~/.config/scd\-reporting/.env
Per-user \fB.env\fR file.
.TP
.I ./.env
Per-directory \fB.env\fR file.
.SH NOTES
All tools use only the Python standard library (PyYAML is used for the config file when installed,
otherwise a simple \fBkey: value\fR reader). Python 3.9 or later. On Windows run them through the
interpreter, e.g. \fBpy scripts\\scd\-report \-f md\fR or \fBpy scripts\\scd_client.py report \-f md\fR.
.SH EXAMPLES
Markdown report of DUNE work last month:
.PP
.nf
.RS
scd\-report \-p dune \-\-period last\-month > dune\-oct.md
.RE
.fi
.PP
Everything touching a date range, as Excel:
.PP
.nf
.RS
scd\-report \-\-from 2026\-10\-01 \-\-to 2026\-10\-31 \-\-overlap \-f xlsx \-o oct.xlsx
.RE
.fi
.PP
How many DAQ entries this quarter mention both timing and trigger:
.PP
.nf
.RS
scd\-report \-p mu2e\-daq \-s 'timing AND "trigger"' \-\-period this\-quarter \-\-count
.RE
.fi
.PP
Pipe JSON into jq:
.PP
.nf
.RS
scd\-report \-f json \-\-period last\-week | jq '.[].title'
.RE
.fi
